# par Noir — North star (THE problem)

This is why the repo exists. Local bugfixes that weaken this goal are wrong even if they compile.

## THE problem

Digital (and now AI) civilization has **no human root** — so every layer of power recentralizes away from persons. Platforms and AIs become principals; humans become the resource. Automation + AI collapsing barriers will amplify that unless persons are Layer 1 of the stack the world actually runs on — with privacy and speech as protocol defaults, not platform permissions.

## What we are building

A **human → AI** substrate (symbiosis, not replacement):

| Primitive | Decentralizes |
|---|---|
| Identity | who you are |
| Dashboard + custody | how you hold data |
| Pen | what you make (humans + agents, one IR) |
| Browse | what you share (public) |
| Messaging | how you communicate (private) |
| Licensing / creator value | how ordinary activity can pay the person |
| API → L5 | how others build on user infrastructure without re-centralizing |

**Invert the model:** value flows to users for things they already do (share, engage, create, license), in forms they understand — not extract-into-platform pools. Agents co-create *on* human custody; they are not landlords.

## Agent obligations (every task)

Before implementing, answer (briefly, to yourself):

1. Which primitive/layer is this?
2. Does this strengthen **human-as-root**, or create a landlord shortcut (app DB SoT, trust-the-client, agent-owned silo, soft-null on a credential path)?
3. Is there already a canonical module in `packages/` / API — or are we about to fork?
4. What **falsifies** done? (user-visible symptom + no dual path)

### Do

- Prefer **delete + rebuild** when the path’s architecture is wrong — see `rebuild-not-patch.mdc`
- Trace credential/storage paths to the **external boundary** — see `diagnostic-discipline.mdc`
- Keep apps thin; shared behavior in `packages/` — see `how-to-build.mdc`
- Encode new invariants in check scripts / gate tests — see `enforcement.mdc`

### Do not

- Ship **incomplete routes** (silent `return null`, verify-later stubs, “works for happy path only” auth/custody)
- Add **shims, dual resolvers, JSON/API fallbacks, compat re-exports** next to a fix
- Optimize for “minimal diff” when the architecture is wrong
- Build **AI-first parallel kingdoms** (separate agent content model, agent-owned memory silo, bypass of Pen/custody)
- Treat monetization, Pen, messaging, or browse as unrelated products — they are one stack under identity

## Done

Not “tests pass” alone. Done = the user-visible acceptance holds **and** the path has one clear architecture with no dead dual. If verification was skipped or blocked, the plan is void — say so; do not declare success.
